{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039988-twilight-question","id":1039988,"title":"Twilight question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-29T07:59:50-08:00","id":1039988,"title":"Twilight question","content":"The spiritual aspects of CofD are in no way my strong suits, so I thought I should ask about it here.<br /> <br /> A Thyrsus Banisher flees from a Moros Adamantine Arrow. The Thyrsus uses Spirit to shift into twilight. The Moros sees this and uses Death to also step into twilight. Can these two now see each other in twilight? The rulebook, Mage at least, specifically mentions that the spells for stepping into twilight turns the caster into ephemera. Does the Thyrsus thus register as a &quot;spirit&quot; and the Moros as a &quot;ghost&quot;, necesitating the proper Arcana to spot each other?<br /> <br /> In my games I have ruled that two mages (or two physical beings in general) in twilight can always see each other, unless there are supernatural stealth effects going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9849,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","user":"Aristarkos","date":". 01-29-2017, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T08:02:47-08:00","id":1039991,"title":"","content":"By RAW, no. However, you did state that you ruled that they could see each other regardless, so you're answer would be yes, you can still track the Banisher through into Twilight. A good question is, can they interact with one another?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T08:29:40-08:00","id":1039999,"title":"","content":"RAW they can neither interact with nor perceive each other. That's the point of having different phases of Twilight.<br /> Neither would register as a ghost or spirit - they would register as Death-attuned Ephemera or Spirit-attuned Ephemera.<br /> <br /> Edit: I might be wrong about perception. The books aren't explicit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 01-29-2017, 11:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T08:51:19-08:00","id":1040012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039988-twilight-question?p=1039999#post1039999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RAW they can neither interact with nor perceive each other. That's the point of having different phases of Twilight.<br /> Neither would register as a ghost or spirit - they would register as Death-attuned Ephemera or Spirit-attuned Ephemera.<br /> <br /> Edit: I might be wrong about perception. The books aren't explicit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You are not wrong Death-Attuned can only see other Death-Attuned and same for Spirit-Attuned, this also applies to the interacting with each other. And of course this is RAW, how you do it in your game is entirely up to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T08:57:55-08:00","id":1040016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039988-twilight-question?p=1039999#post1039999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RAW they can neither interact with nor perceive each other. That's the point of having different phases of Twilight.<br /> Neither would register as a ghost or spirit - they would register as Death-attuned Ephemera or Spirit-attuned Ephemera.<br /> <br /> Edit: I might be wrong about perception. The books aren't explicit.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're correct as far as I know.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9849_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9849\" data-vbnamecard=\"9849\">Aristarkos</a>: Remember that twilight a state of being - saying something is &quot;in twilight&quot; is the same as saying it's &quot;out of phase&quot; or &quot;incorporeal&quot;. Like radio waves, objects and entities in the state of twilight have different frequencies, and can only interact with each other when they are attuned to the same frequency. So, the Mage Thyrsus puts himself into the state of twilight with a spell from the Spirit Arcanum, which means his metaphysical &quot;wavelength&quot; is the same as the &quot;wavelength&quot; of a non-materialized spirit. He isn't actually a spirit and doesn't register as one, he's just tuned to the same station that spirits are. <br /> <br /> Likewise, the Moros uses the Death Arcanum to phase himself out, putting him in the same frequency of twilight as non-materialized ghosts. Not a ghost himself, but on the same wavelength as ghosts. They can't see or interact with each other, and more than a materialized entity can see and interact with either of them, because they're all resonating at different frequencies.<br /> <br /> And as everyone has been saying, feel free to run it whatever way works best for you. Just letting you know the RAW since you asked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-29-2017, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T09:27:57-08:00","id":1040038,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> national non-materialized spirit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T09:32:35-08:00","id":1040044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039988-twilight-question?p=1040038#post1040038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> national non-materialized spirit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure how national got in there. Auto-correct does some weird shit sometimes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T09:34:11-08:00","id":1040046,"title":"","content":"A strange place, that would be. Here, the only nationalized spirits are at the LCBO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T10:03:03-08:00","id":1040069,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much for the answers, nationalized or not!<br /> <br /> These RAW rules make sense, even though my players will frown upon me changing the rules from previous games.<br /> <br /> Another question, if you may: when angels and God-Machine servitors step into twilight, what are their ephemera? Infrastructure? And what Arcana would a mage need to see and interact with them? Prime?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9849,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","user":"Aristarkos","date":". 01-29-2017, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T12:20:27-08:00","id":1040135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039988-twilight-question?p=1040016#post1040016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're correct as far as I know.<br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>: Remember that twilight a state of being - saying something is &amp;quot;in twilight&amp;quot; is the same as saying it's &amp;quot;out of phase&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;incorporeal&amp;quot;. Like radio waves, objects and entities in the state of twilight have different frequencies, and can only interact with each other when they are attuned to the same frequency. So, the Mage Thyrsus puts himself into the state of twilight with a spell from the Spirit Arcanum, which means his metaphysical &amp;quot;wavelength&amp;quot; is the same as the &amp;quot;wavelength&amp;quot; of a non-materialized spirit. He isn't actually a spirit and doesn't register as one, he's just tuned to the same station that spirits are. <br /> <br /> Likewise, the Moros uses the Death Arcanum to phase himself out, putting him in the same frequency of twilight as non-materialized ghosts. Not a ghost himself, but on the same wavelength as ghosts. They can't see or interact with each other, and more than a materialized entity can see and interact with either of them, because they're all resonating at different frequencies.<br /> <br /> And as everyone has been saying, feel free to run it whatever way works best for you. Just letting you know the RAW since you asked.</div> </div> </div> </div>So would Speak to the Dead or the equivalent spirit spell let a mage see either of the other mages in twilight, albeit recognizing that they are not ghosts/spirits? Or would it take a different application of Death/Spirit to perceive them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T12:51:22-08:00","id":1040157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039988-twilight-question?p=1040135#post1040135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So would Speak to the Dead or the equivalent spirit spell let a mage see either of the other mages in twilight, albeit recognizing that they are not ghosts/spirits? Or would it take a different application of Death/Spirit to perceive them?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really going to come down to your table. I'd require a separate spell or a Reach effect, personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T13:12:34-08:00","id":1040166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039988-twilight-question?p=1040135#post1040135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So would Speak to the Dead or the equivalent spirit spell let a mage see either of the other mages in twilight, albeit recognizing that they are not ghosts/spirits? Or would it take a different application of Death/Spirit to perceive them?</div> </div> </div> </div>What Inodiv said. That's down to an ST call, and I'd say it's definitely reasonable as a +1 Reach effect. I would rule that the Death 1 Attainment Eyes of the Dead would definitely allow someone to see the twilight Moros, since it lets you perceive &quot;ghosts and deathly Twilight phenomena&quot;. I'd say the Mage in this scenario counts as an other deathly twilight phenomenon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T13:24:51-08:00","id":1040175,"title":"","content":"For me it's not even a Reach effect. It's part of a Speak to the XXX spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T14:04:41-08:00","id":1040202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039988-twilight-question?p=1040069#post1040069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you very much for the answers, nationalized or not!<br /> <br /> These RAW rules make sense, even though my players will frown upon me changing the rules from previous games.<br /> <br /> Another question, if you may: when angels and God-Machine servitors step into twilight, what are their ephemera? Infrastructure? And what Arcana would a mage need to see and interact with them? Prime?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I understand the rules on Supernal Entities correctly when they enter Twilight it is just like a mage, whatever power they used to enter twilight is what they are attuned to, for example if a Supernal Entity used a death spell (remember Supernal Entities have Arcanum just as mages do) then they are Death-Attuned and would see and interact with Ghost and other stuff attuned to Death.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T14:07:12-08:00","id":1040204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039988-twilight-question?p=1040202#post1040202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I understand the rules on Supernal Entities correctly when they enter Twilight it is just like a mage, whatever power they used to enter twilight is what they are attuned to, for example if a Supernal Entity used a death spell (remember Supernal Entities have Arcanum just as mages do) then they are Death-Attuned and would see and interact with Ghost and other stuff attuned to Death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Angels and God-Machine being referenced are not Supernal Entities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T14:10:35-08:00","id":1040206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039988-twilight-question?p=1040204#post1040204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Angels and God-Machine being referenced are not Supernal Entities.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well there you go, then I don't know the answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T12:11:14-08:00","id":1040807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039988-twilight-question?p=1040069#post1040069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question, if you may: when angels and God-Machine servitors step into twilight, what are their ephemera? Infrastructure? And what Arcana would a mage need to see and interact with them? Prime?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty fond of Space for Angel/GM stuff, since it's all Sympathy to me.<br /> I think Dave's most recent input on the subject was Prime/Fate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T18:07:50-08:00","id":1041009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039988-twilight-question?p=1040807#post1040807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty fond of Space for Angel/GM stuff, since it's all Sympathy to me.<br /> I think Dave's most recent input on the subject was Prime/Fate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Prime &amp; Spirit from my memory. The former governs the underlying mechanisms of the world described in occult trappings, and the latter governs the relationships between various actors of the world that are expressed as resonance.<br /> <br /> That, and how the divine were traditionally associated with Prime, while Spirit seems to be the go-to for ephemeral entities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T22:58:57-08:00","id":1041114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039988-twilight-question?p=1041009#post1041009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Prime &amp; Spirit from my memory. The former governs the underlying mechanisms of the world described in occult trappings, and the latter governs the relationships between various actors of the world that are expressed as resonance.<br /> <br /> That, and how the divine were traditionally associated with Prime, while Spirit seems to be the go-to for ephemeral entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was his original suggestion, but it was revised to Prime/Fate in a later post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T15:27:38-08:00","id":1041519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039988-twilight-question?p=1041114#post1041114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was his original suggestion, but it was revised to Prime/Fate in a later post.</div> </div> </div> </div>Must have missed that one. Strange, since I still think Spirit fits better than Fate. Oh well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T22:07:11-08:00","id":1041688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbco